      "message": "Same account, two codes: a disabled user gets 401 at /login (verify_password returns False -\u003e basic_auth 401) but 403 on check_access routes. Both reject, which is what matters. The snag is the login response is identical to a wrong password, so a disabled user just sees \u0027Unauthorized Access\u0027 with no hint the account is disabled. Suggest a distinct signal, or at least a README note that a disabled account surfaces as 401 at /login and 403 on the API.",
